cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Glenn.jl in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "Glenn.jl: NASA-7 thermochemical properties in Julia"
abstract: >-
  Glenn.jl provides Cp(T), H°(T) and S°(T) for 2035 species by evaluating the
  NASA-7 polynomial coefficients of the NASA Glenn CEA thermodynamic database,
  which is bundled as an SQLite file so that no configuration is required.
  The package offers species lookup, mixtures, sensible- and total-enthalpy
  helpers, analytic Cp derivatives, a database integrity validator, a
  least-squares fitter for NASA-7 coefficients, and a command-line interface
  for building and inspecting databases. Results are cross-validated against
  the NIST-JANAF Thermochemical Tables for seven reference species.
